  "title": "Cape Hatteras Lighthouse",
  "summary": "The Cape Hatteras Lighthouse at Buxton, North Carolina, was lit on 16 December 1870 to warn ships off the Diamond Shoals sandbar. The National Park Service calls it the tallest brick lighthouse in the United States, at 198.49 feet including the foundation. It was moved 2,900 feet inland because of shoreline erosion.",
